<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<chapter xml:id="ch-6-Interludes" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
    <title>Interludes</title>

    <introduction component="not-workbook">
        <p>
			Like the prelude chapter, the sections in this interlude chapter are intended to be covered in between or alongside sections in previous chapters.  In a later edition of the textbook, they will be interwoven as needed.
		</p>

		<p>
			Notes (to instructors):
			
			<ul>
				<li>
					<p>
						<xref ref="sec-6-1-First_look_polynomials" text="type-global-title"/> is a full day's lesson.  It can be covered after
						<xref ref="sec-2-1-First_look_linear" text="type-global-title"/>
						and ideally before 
						<xref ref="sec-2-3-Using_equations" text="type-global-title"/>.  
						A natural place would be between 
						<xref ref="sec-2-2-First_look_exponential" text="global"/>
						and 
						<xref ref="sec-2-3-Using_equations" text="global"/>.
					</p>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<xref ref="sec-6-2-First_look_right_triangles" text="type-global-title"/> is a half day's lesson.  It is needed before 7.1 Right triangles, and possibly would fit the same day as 7.1.  The intent was that 6.2 be covered alongside 
						<xref ref="sec-3-3-Solving_power_equations" text="type-global-title"/>
						especially if 
						<xref ref="sec-0-6-Powers_and_roots" text="type-global-title"/>
						is covered separately.
					</p>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<xref ref="sec-6-3-piecewise-linear" text="type-global-title"/>
						is another half day's lesson. It naturally fits alongside 
						<xref ref="sec-4-1-Modeling_linear_equations" text="type-global-title"/>, 
						which is otherwise a very short review section.
					</p>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<xref ref="sec-6-4-Point-slope_form" text="type-global-title"/>
						is a full day's lesson.  It should be covered after 
						<xref ref="sec-4-4-Slopes" text="type-global-title"/>
						It would fit best after 
						<xref ref="sec-4-5-Fitting_lines_to_data" text="global"/>,
						if that section is covered.
					</p>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>
						<xref ref="sec-6-5-Linear_vs_exp_point-slope" text="type-global-title"/>
						is a half day's lesson.  It is intended to be an addendum to 
						<xref ref="sec-5-4-Linear_vs_exponential" text="type-global-title"/>,
						perhaps replacing 
						<xref ref="bus-fares-linear-exponential" text="custom">
							5.4 #4
						</xref>
						in the workbook with 
						<xref ref="parents-house-lve-point-slope" text="custom">
							6.5 #1
						</xref>.
					</p>
				</li>
			</ul>
		</p>
    </introduction>

	<xi:include href="./sec-6-1-First_look_polynomials.ptx" />
	<xi:include href="./sec-6-2-First_look_right_triangles.ptx" />
	<xi:include href="./sec-6-3-Piecewise_linear.ptx" />
	<xi:include href="./sec-6-4-Point-slope_form.ptx" />
	<xi:include href="./sec-6-5-Linear_vs_exp_point-slope.ptx" />

	<!-- practice exams? surely not -->
</chapter>